<tool id="abricate_list" name="ABRicate List" version="1.4.0+galaxy0">
  <description>List Antibiotic Resistance Genes Databases</description>
  <macros />
  <xrefs>
    <xref type="bio.tools">abricate</xref>
  </xrefs>
  <requirements>
    <requirement type="package" version="1.4.0">abricate</requirement>
  </requirements>
  <command detect_errors="exit_code">
abricate --list
    </command>
  <inputs />
  <outputs>
    <data name="output" format="tabular" label="${tool.name} on ${on_string}: Antibiotic Resistance Genes Databases" />
  </outputs>
  <tests>
    <test>
      <output name="output">
        <assert_contents>
          <has_line line="aac(6')-aph(2'')" count="1" />
          <has_line line="aadD" count="1" />
          <has_line line="blaZ_32" count="1" />
          <has_line line="blaZ_36" count="1" />
          <has_line line="erm(A)" count="1" />
          <has_line line="mecA_15" count="1" />
          <has_line line="norA_1" count="1" />
          <has_line line="spc_1" count="1" />
          <has_line line="tet(M)" count="1" />
        </assert_contents>
      </output>
    </test>
  </tests>
  <help>
**What it does**

ABRicate List will list all the antibiotic databases used by ABRicate. The database of these genes is built from ResFinder.

    </help>
  <citations>
    <citation type="doi">10.1093/bioinformatics/btz005</citation>
    <citation type="bibtex">@misc{galaxy_toolsmith,
  title = {Galaxy Toolsmith},
  howpublished = {\url{https://github.com/BlankenbergLab/galaxy-toolsmith}},
  url = {https://github.com/BlankenbergLab/galaxy-toolsmith}
}</citation>
  </citations>
</tool>